0..43 Comment "//! Rose trees use direct and mutual forms."
44..47 Comment "//!"
48..89 Comment "//! `Bush` stores its children in `List`."
90..134 Comment "//! The list parameter is strictly positive."
135..191 Comment "//! Its measure maps over the children at a lower stage."
192..195 Comment "//!"
196..242 Comment "//! `Rose` and `Forest` form one mutual block."
243..279 Comment "//! Their measures share a fixpoint."
280..334 Comment "//! The mutual measures keep a later weight parameter."
335..389 Comment "//! Each recursive call uses a smaller tree or forest."
390..393 Comment "//!"
394..462 Comment "//! - see: #3722 — a measure keeps a parameter in its sibling call"
463..489 Comment "//! - see: #517 — `Bush`"
490..517 Comment "//! - see: #393 — `nodes`"
518..566 Comment "//! - see: #452 — `shrub_nodes`, `grown_nodes`"
